  "rationale": "For 2026-03-31, the filing's fund-level schedule shows total investments of $1,246,701 thousand cost and $1,249,444 thousand fair value, while the separately dimensioned nonconsolidated-subsidiary portfolio schedule shows $234,025 thousand principal, $231,731 thousand cost, and $231,531 thousand fair value. The extracted holdings show 71 rows carrying the AGL EPCI II nonconsolidated-subsidiary dimension; their principal and fair value sum exactly to $234,025,000 and $231,531,000, respectively, but extracted exposure_type is DIRECT for all 71. Extracted all-row fair value is therefore $1,480,975,000 versus the filing's fund-level $1,249,444,000, a difference of exactly $231,531,000. The filing shows these rows at the subsidiary portfolio layer, while extracted shows them as DIRECT; setting exposure_type to INDIRECT on the exact rebuild-stable row IDs corrects the look-through classification without changing reported amounts. One separate extraction discrepancy remains outside this classification fix: extracted subsidiary-row cost sums to $243,755,000 rather than the filing's $231,731,000 because one Flexera row carries $12,184,000 extracted cost despite a dash in the subsidiary schedule; no numeric value is changed by this template.",
